Has poco https also instead of http?

Yes. **POCO supports HTTPS** as well as HTTP.

With POCO Net, you can create:

* `Poco::Net::HTTPServer` → HTTP server
* `Poco::Net::HTTPServer` + `SecureServerSocket` → **HTTPS server**

Typical POCO HTTPS setup:

```cpp
#include <Poco/Net/HTTPServer.h>
#include <Poco/Net/SecureServerSocket.h>

using namespace Poco::Net;

SecureServerSocket socket(8443);
HTTPServer server(new MyRequestHandlerFactory, socket, new HTTPServerParams);

server.start();
```

Then your C++ API can be accessed directly as:

```text
https://localhost:8443/api/hello
```

### So you have two architectures

**1. TLS termination at Nginx — common**

```text
Client
  │ HTTPS
  ▼
Nginx :443
  │ HTTP
  ▼
POCO :8080
```

**2. HTTPS all the way**

```text
Client
  │ HTTPS
  ▼
Nginx :443
  │ HTTPS
  ▼
POCO :8443
```

For your **POCO + Nginx REST API**, I'd normally start with **#1**. 
Nginx handles certificates/TLS, while your POCO application stays focused on the REST API.
